    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1155" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aedŭi</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haed-</span></b> ), ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a tribe in Gallia
				Celtica friendly to the Romans</i>, now <i>Departements de la Cōte d'Or</i>, <i>de
				la Nievre</i>, 
			
			<i>de Saōne et Loire</i>, <i>et
				du Rhōne</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes.
				B. G. 1, 10, 11, 23</span></i>, etc.; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 1,
				19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4,
				18, 32, § 107 al.</span></i>—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aedŭĭ-cus</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haed-</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>pertaining to the Ædui</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stemma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Par. 4, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
